! REPRODUCER, a MODEL finding (docs/NEXT.md, "G2.1 CHAPTER 4: LOCATION 8
! AS A FLOATING-POINT OPERAND TAKES THE WRONG SIGN").
!
! Reference Manual printed p.37 (PDF 40), "Accumulator and Sign Byte
! Register": "The accumulator may also be addressed as an operand in
! storage.  When location 8, the left half of the accumulator, is
! explicitly addressed as the operand in a floating point operation, a
! word is obtained that consists of bits 0-59 of the accumulator
! followed by bits 4-7 of the accumulator sign byte, thus forming a
! proper floating point word."
!
! So with -1/2 in the accumulator, "*(N), $L" squares it: +1/4.
!   PROD = +.25 = exponent -1, fraction .5 = 0038 0000 0000 0000.
! The model reads word 8's own bits 60-63 as the operand's sign byte.
! Those are accumulator fraction bits 48-51, zero after DL (printed
! p.96), so it multiplies -1/2 by +1/2:
!   PROD = 0038 0000 0000 0008, -1/4.   OBSERVED 2026-11-16.
! The control, +1/2 squared, is right either way, 0038 0000 0000 0000.
!
! The halves are written "1X0" (1 = .5 x 2**1, X replacing the exponent
! with 0; C28-6129 printed p.27), which is exactly 1/2.  ".5" is not:
! STRAP II's DNUM makes it 5 x (1/10 truncated), one unit below 1/2 in
! 48 bits (C22-6729 pp.108-111; docs/NEXT.md, "DD(N) 1.0 IS 1 - 2^-48
! UNDER STRAP II"), and both assemblers now say so.  Changed 2026-11-16.
!
! Found by C22-6578 Problem 4.10, printed p.44, "*(N), $L  'Z**2", which
! squares a negative Z whenever x's fraction is below 1/sqrt2
! (decks/problem_4_10.strap).

START   DL(N), MHALF
        *(N), $L
        ST(U), PROD
        DL(N), PHALF
        *(N), $L
        ST(U), CTRL
HALT    BEW, $
MHALF   DD(N), -1X0
PHALF   DD(N), 1X0
PROD    DD(BU,64,8), 7
CTRL    DD(BU,64,8), 7
        END, START
